<h2>Step 1: Read</h2>

<p>
  Start by reading the Bible consistently and repeatedly. For the Old Testament, read through it
  at least once a year in a narrative fashion. Make notes in the margins, and write down anything
  you don&rsquo;t immediately understand. Many questions will be answered by the text itself as
  you keep reading.
</p>

<p>
  For the New Testament, try a different approach: read one book at a time, repetitiously, for
  thirty days straight. Start with a short book like 1 John and read it all the way through in
  one sitting every day for a month. By the end, you will know that book. For longer books like
  John, divide it into three sections of seven chapters and read each section daily for thirty
  days. In less than three years you can know the entire New Testament this way. There is no
  substitute for this kind of immersive, repeated reading.
</p>

